examples.question_text:
Find the radius of this circle. Give your answer in centimetres as a decimal and as a fraction.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.8);
\draw (0,-1.8)--(0,1.8);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,0.85) node[right,fill=white,inner sep=2pt] {$11\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The marked line passes through the centre and joins two points on the circumference, so it is a diameter. Divide it by $2$.

$\begin{aligned}r &= \frac{d}{2}\\ &= \frac{11}{2}\text{ cm}\\ &= 5.5\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$

The radius is $5.5\text{ cm}$, or $\frac{11}{2}\text{ cm}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.8);
\draw (0,-1.8)--(0,1.8);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,0.9) node[right,fill=white,inner sep=2pt] {$5.5\text{ cm}$};
\path (0,-0.9) node[right,fill=white,inner sep=2pt] {$5.5\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

